  "response_text": "A queue is interesting because it isn\u2019t an array. The queue has a benefit as it takes up less space as everything will be stored beside each other in memory. The thread will dequeue from the front of the queue and run that thread then after it has finished running it would queue it at the back of the queue and repeat the process. This allows for more efficient use as if a thread ever needs to be removed you don\u2019t need to move things around in the array and everything will get equal treatment.\\n",
